.\"
.\" OPEN(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH OPEN 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
open, creat \- open and possibly create a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fcntl.h>
.PP
.BI "int open(const char *" pathname ", int " flags ");
.BI "int open(const char *" pathname ", int " flags ", mode_t " mode ");
.BI "int creat(const char *" pathname ", mode_t " mode ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR open ()
system call opens the file specified by
.IR pathname .
If the specified file does not exist, it may optionally be created
(if
.B O_CREAT
is specified in
.IR flags ).
.PP
The
.I flags
argument must include one of the following access modes:
.BR O_RDONLY ", " O_WRONLY ", or " O_RDWR .
.SS Flags
.TP
.B O_RDONLY
Open for reading only.
.TP
.B O_WRONLY
Open for writing only.
.TP
.B O_RDWR
Open for reading and writing.
.TP
.B O_CREAT
If the file does not exist, create it.
.TP
.B O_TRUNC
If the file exists, truncate it to length 0.
.TP
.B O_APPEND
Append mode.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, the new file descriptor is returned.
.PP
On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOENT
.I pathname
does not exist and
.B O_CREAT
was not specified.
.TP
.B EACCES
Access denied.
.TP
.B EMFILE
Too many open files.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 5 (SYS_OPEN)
Arguments:      pathname, flags, mode (on stack)

    push mode
    push flags
    push pathname
    push $0
    mov eax, 5
    int $0x80
    add esp, 16
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR close (2),
.BR read (2),
.BR write (2),
.BR stat (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
